WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.680
Hey everyone, привет, welcome to привет русский эпизод 39 for 14 июня 2026 года.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.540
I am allia, today's lesson is going to be a fun one.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:12.540
Коехали?

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:17.220
Today our word of the day is хлеб, хлеб, хлеб.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.800
Say it slowly with me, хлеб.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.080
It sounds a little like club, but means bread.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.480
Imagine a warm love fresh from the oven.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.080
Russian's call bread the stuff of life.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.880
Now repeat after me, хлеб.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.300
Now say it faster, хлеб.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.040
Я ем хлеб, я ем хлеб.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.740
That means I eat bread.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.980
Our lesson today is all about food words.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.580
Let's build a vocabulary step by step.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.360
First we have молоко, молоко.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:48.680
That means milk.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.460
Repeat after me, молоко.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.620
Now say it faster, молоко.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.780
Кот пьет молоко, кот пьет молоко.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:56.940
The cat drinks milk.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.540
Remember кошка from a few lessons ago.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.240
Кошка means cat.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.440
Next comes сыр, сыр.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:04.700
That means cheese.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.560
Repeat after me, сыр.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.580
Now faster, сыр, сыр вкусный.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.280
The cheese is delicious.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.040
Сир раем с водстор.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.180
Стор the cheese into your meal.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.800
Now we meet яблоко, яблоко.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.200
That means apple.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:20.880
Repeat after me, яблоко.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.240
Now faster, яблоко.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:24.960
Я люблю яблоко.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.000
I love an apple.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.100
Яблоко starts like yap.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.880
А док might yap for an apple.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.600
Next is water, вода.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:33.980
That means water.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.840
Repeat after me, вода.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:37.840
Now faster, вода.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:39.800
Пей воду, drink water.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.860
Вода sounds like vodka without the fun part.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.240
It is just plain water.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.120
Here is чай, чай.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.220
That means tea.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.860
Repeat after me, чай.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.340
Now faster, чай.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.540
Чай горячий, that is hot.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.660
Чай sounds exactly like tea and chai tea.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:56.940
You already know it.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.260
Now we learn мясо, мясо.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.100
That means meat, repeat after me, мясо.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.560
Now faster, мясо.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.900
мясо на тарелке, meat is on the plate.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.840
мясо starts like my, my favorite meat.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.280
Next come овощи, овощки.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:14.700
That means vegetables, repeat after me, овощки.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.440
Now faster, овощки.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.320
Овощки полезные, водитables are healthy.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.380
Овощки, овощки, овощки.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.260
Маневодитables are oval shaped.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.520
Here are fructы, fructы, that means fruit.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.460
Repeat after me, fructы.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.460
Now faster, fructы, fructы сладкие, fructы are sweet.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:36.420
Фрукты sounds almost like fructи, exactly what it means.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.160
Finally we have yeast, yeast.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.220
That means to eat, repeat after me, yeast.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.160
Now faster, yeast.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.160
Я ем хлеб, я eat bread, yeast sounds like yeast.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.640
Yes, I want to eat.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.900
Рашен nouns have gender.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.740
They can be masculine, feminine or neuter.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.040
Food words show this clearly.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.300
хлеб is masculine because it ends in a consonant.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.660
Малако is neuter because it ends in O.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.920
Вода is feminine because it ends in A.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.420
In English we do not change words this way.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.760
In Russian you match adjective to the noun gender.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.840
Вкусный хлеб is masculine.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.020
Вкусная молоко is neuter.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.840
Вкусная вода is feminine.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.780
The ending of the adjective changes too much.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.060
Now you can describe foods correctly.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.780
In Russia, tea is more than a drink.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.140
It is a daily ritual of hospitality.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.320
Families gather around the sumover.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.400
A sumover is a special metal urn.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.660
They drink strong tea with jam, lemon or sweets.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.640
Offering tea to guests says you are welcome here.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.840
Do you remember what хлеб means?

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:43.880
It means bread.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.520
Try saying tea three times today.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.740
For kids, draw your favorite food.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.660
Label it with the Russian word.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.660
Try хлеб or яблоко.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.860
For adults say the Russian names at breakfast.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.920
Say я ем хлеб и пью чай, while you prepare it.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.720
Want to know a secret about tea?

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.180
Did you know that the Russian word чай

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.980
and the English word чай are actually the same word?

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.440
They both come from the Chinese word for tea, чай.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.820
This word started in China.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:16.500
It traveled along the ancient Silk Road through Central Asia.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.880
It was borrowed into Russian in the 17th century.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:23.220
Later it reached English as чай through trade.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.420
But be careful, the Russian word magazine sounds like magazine,

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.380
but actually means shop.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.360
Next time you see чай on a menu, remember it is cousins with чай.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.740
They both come from Chinese, чай.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:39.260
That connection is your secret shortcut

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:40.840
to remembering it forever.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.780
And that's our lesson for today.

